[{:db/id "q-346546/field-1/6958c15362a7b3feefba93a61d0fe19a013cb3cca50a0ab1808de3ac0d59606c" :answer/id #uuid "3bace1ab-1f8b-564a-965f-6880a8a258e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346546/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd544d3-dbff-5f3e-8c77-9b66d9c3f746" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346546/field-1/6958c15362a7b3feefba93a61d0fe19a013cb3cca50a0ab1808de3ac0d59606c" :answer-field/choices ["q-346546/field-1/6958c15362a7b3feefba93a61d0fe19a013cb3cca50a0ab1808de3ac0d59606c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346546" :question/id #uuid "66b34e07-5d41-5462-a3f4-96722a374f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-346546" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14\\cdot 1-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(14x-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[14\\pi -\\frac{5}{3}{\\pi }^{3}]-[14\\cdot 0-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}] \\\\  & =14\\pi -\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346546/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49447"] :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10{cos}^{2}⁡x-4{x}^{3}+10{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10{cos}^{2}⁡x-4{x}^{3}+10{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10\\cdot 1-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(10x-{x}^{4}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}]-[10\\cdot 0-{0}^{4}] \\\\  & =10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-51122"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-346553/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d00c951d-4a39-5aab-a6a1-0ccdcc82cfcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346553/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "13fd5c80-454b-525a-9fe8-963eb6b13b11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346553/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb19355b-d581-52c3-b921-82e5ecfd04a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346553/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-346553/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-346553/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346553" :question/id #uuid "48131121-0026-58df-8189-363af1e15829" :question/math-academy-id "q-346553" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346553/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352619/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "5d209727-3ea2-5344-ad37-042a92270fff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352619/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "226c9f98-5538-5736-abd8-c715a703c5f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352619/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-352619/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352619" :question/id #uuid "7625b3b6-4dc7-571c-abe3-9b10fecadd83" :question/math-academy-id "q-352619" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =2(2-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352619/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352619"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114429/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "61860341-235f-5057-86fe-392354a1d2d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114429/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "11b581b1-dbf4-5bf7-ba17-0c5256c868e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114429/selection/bc4d6c8210bf50076f59415fb6a33e7562cff30effbc15182a04baaf4a90e8c7" :answer/id #uuid "b6cd6c4a-72bb-5725-b398-d34c4fc23769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114429/selection/ac9362c9c743a0d4cd03c825418c9d77629147a5815c12295606faadbe8a8744" :answer/id #uuid "3bdcf953-9007-5af8-b288-d362a7ffea51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114429/selection/2b44e6d43e3927389e0c1c2c163b7136f70bbb82b73accf5d4c97d2f0dd2b207" :answer/id #uuid "a43b7419-1adc-5e16-a77c-671d4e3da581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114429/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc79626e-88c9-524b-a498-078cf002195b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114429/selection/2b44e6d43e3927389e0c1c2c163b7136f70bbb82b73accf5d4c97d2f0dd2b207" :answer-field/choices ["q-114429/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-114429/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-114429/selection/bc4d6c8210bf50076f59415fb6a33e7562cff30effbc15182a04baaf4a90e8c7" "q-114429/selection/ac9362c9c743a0d4cd03c825418c9d77629147a5815c12295606faadbe8a8744" "q-114429/selection/2b44e6d43e3927389e0c1c2c163b7136f70bbb82b73accf5d4c97d2f0dd2b207"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114429" :question/id #uuid "825e16c0-50ba-5c9d-83b3-eb1bef11322e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114429" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-[2-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114429/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114429"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186097195 :question/answer-fields 17592186095527] {:db/id "q-49326/selection/ma-v1/f6e53ea1fd91b5ef59ca45ce0a4c63c849654a855cfde31a7a86097a416d1790/a1718737dbd495fb450a9cad74f457749b10e8bf5f8306a2293022758aa6513c" :answer/id #uuid "e443089c-2478-57d4-8b61-a32aceb0d097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49326/selection/ma-v1/f6e53ea1fd91b5ef59ca45ce0a4c63c849654a855cfde31a7a86097a416d1790/0d493251931cc605e892db74e058983a8bd88db494d0e39af4dca97c0964b1b2" :answer/id #uuid "d0aabeb1-1092-5f4c-9079-936d9396f514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49326/selection/ma-v1/f6e53ea1fd91b5ef59c