a855cfde31a7a86097a416d1790/c2cd5706703cb5dabbf0f09b3eecdd15e6abcb88bab4a483ca636073fbd7f7ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49326"] :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. We can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-9(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-49326/selection/ma-v1/f6e53ea1fd91b5ef59ca45ce0a4c63c849654a855cfde31a7a86097a416d1790"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-352644/field-1/070867f5baebecc015e0aac56a86285e1008deea8637d6922deae79a2bea8a5e" :answer/id #uuid "9d2ea12a-1c77-57bc-a37d-1f1d2df90d03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352644/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "e52d3b22-a3be-59e0-95d5-e5d23247e714" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352644/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "59adba1c-cab2-5d55-8e88-ff1488affea9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352644/field-1/070867f5baebecc015e0aac56a86285e1008deea8637d6922deae79a2bea8a5e" :answer-field/choices ["q-352644/field-1/070867f5baebecc015e0aac56a86285e1008deea8637d6922deae79a2bea8a5e" "q-352644/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352644" :question/id #uuid "51dac45a-d3d2-569a-91fe-6eed04fa0935" :question/math-academy-id "q-352644" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So, we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352644/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-10563"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 100{tan}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 100{tan}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 100({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (100{sec}^{2}⁡x-100)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-114431/selection/94bd252c0702de04bd8ec8bd15716ecb55696fa8c1d701dfe696444af333a7a3" :answer/id #uuid "ba623cba-56f4-5df2-b01e-c89e6da70737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114431/selection/f5ec7c64138286a7b0b842bde9873a25341daead6cdc06433efb55f216d464c2" :answer/id #uuid "09f08408-07e3-51bf-81a8-4d328dc4622d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114431/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" :answer/id #uuid "521b454f-144c-56ed-96fe-676dffc1806e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114431/selection/bb506cf003879770dcc37d3f108f66837df546bd68c5ad9b0e1b3a27b8c6ec6c" :answer/id #uuid "2c81d743-b67d-55ae-a037-b2650a6a1e04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114431/selection/4db7b6acb9a12029c5ee221cc89aa6b6e99afe642c66a6524f826023249f0403" :answer/id #uuid "66a798ad-9c17-5c02-b9d8-d476288e0e89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114431/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "14509ddb-e9c7-523b-843a-eaadbcbd2448" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114431/selection/bb506cf003879770dcc37d3f108f66837df546bd68c5ad9b0e1b3a27b8c6ec6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-114431/selection/94bd252c0702de04bd8ec8bd15716ecb55696fa8c1d701dfe696444af333a7a3" "q-114431/selection/f5ec7c64138286a7b0b842bde9873a25341daead6cdc06433efb55f216d464c2" "q-114431/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" "q-114431/selection/bb506cf003879770dcc37d3f108f66837df546bd68c5ad9b0e1b3a27b8c6ec6c" "q-114431/selection/4db7b6acb9a12029c5ee221cc89aa6b6e99afe642c66a6524f826023249f0403"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114431" :question/id #uuid "0e0b6173-4631-5297-abbd-478176d04666" :question/math-academy-id "q-114431" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114431/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114431"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362530/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "27c67c5d-014c-56ed-a3c5-9673afb7b385" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362530/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fba4696-f9f9-5db0-ada5-9259720f40c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362530/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-362530/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362530" :question/id #uuid "ed8a16d4-8afb-57ef-a48b-2f1ad148005c" :question/math-academy-id "q-362530" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-362530/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362530"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362529/field-1/1c6c26d6db2280312c8e9459a1b4b33b77d6ced5f29478bb0d65adfcf297ffe6" :answer/id #uuid "53271748-ae62-5ea7-b5fe-67619c261e73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362529/field-1/e0796b80d61aadc05bbe8388a6b74ba08a30f4910620da5a5a36351dd4a235b6" :answer/id #uuid "052acb96-eaa7-564f-a57b-a720ffe2bb1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362529/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c7fc796-b932-534f-9041-3f809ba61e7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362529/field-1/1c6c26d6db2280312c8e9459a1b4b33b77d6ced5f29478bb0d65adfcf297ffe6" :answer-field/choices ["q-362529/field-1/1c6c26d6db2280312c8e9459a1b4b33b77d6ced5f29478bb0d65adfcf297ffe6" "q-362529/field-1/e0796b80d61aadc05bbe8388a6b74ba08a30f4910620da5a5a36351dd4a235b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362529" :question/id #uuid "7673b5bb-6760-5d7d-840c-35816073b1f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-362529" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3{csc}^{2}⁡x-3{cot}^{2}⁡x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3{csc}^{2}⁡x-3{cot}^{2}⁡x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3({csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x)+4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3(1)+4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+7}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x+7}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+7}-\\sqrt{1+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =3-2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-362529/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362529"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352697/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "238c1871-f4c1-5c75-9465-ff1451c1a319" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352697/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7e44b5-3fa9-5fef-bbf9-f56e43f84dcc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352697/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-352697/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352697" :question/id #uuid "47c77dff-cf5e-5b99-9aa2-2dee7408c956" :question/math-academy-id "q-352697" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the cosecant-cotangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-0-(-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352697/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352697"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114457/selection/a73c5ea78df11c7d4c0ffed5f25a76cdafd8dd5cd7b916f26feb40149cb75ef7" :answer/id #uuid "6d202640-e20a-5db5-82a4-94b92a4173b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114457/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" :answer/id #uuid "d757b342-a58a-5b11-91fe-316c53cb9d2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114457/selection/ab3034954fd3e4244af4bd24c1730574690be4960296a549ee68964a5dc5f6d0" :answer/id #uuid "4d9496f0-7514-5d09-b56e-78bfea78820c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{csc}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114457/selection/9cf685a93656824cec5da2c3f834c523be22f9c78d2da32fe893eed776065f98" :answer/id #uuid "ead2834d-38ea-5328-9472-0a2eb2d0c7b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114457/selection/94bd252c0702de04bd8ec8bd15716ecb55696fa8c1d701dfe696444af333a7a3" :answer/id #uuid "3ee34b64-e8b8-5e21-9a29-56331b10e9c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114457/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23ff2a37-09bc-5179-ad31-0c81b651ae5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114457/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" :answer-field/choices ["q-114457/selection/a73c5ea78df11c7d4c0ffed5f25a76cdafd8dd5cd7b916f26feb40149cb75ef7" "q-114457/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" "q-114457/selection/ab3034954fd3e4244af4bd24c1730574690be4960296a549ee68964a5dc5f6d0" "q-114457/selection/9cf685a93656824cec5da2c3f834c523be22f9c78d2da32fe893eed776065f98" "q-114457/selection/94bd252c0702de04bd8ec8bd15716ecb55696fa8c1d701dfe696444af333a7a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114457" :question/id #uuid "3440293f-c8cd-5460-a9e0-205930295d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114457" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int -\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114457/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362804/field-1/515effaafc563d40e3f20bd9c60358782bd9a05c00761c5732a67ca39f7323bb" :answer/id #uuid "f7ebe951-1980-5a32-bd06-7d0f54a41def" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362804/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bac04891-da67-5498-afd4-620655497049" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362804/field-1/515effaafc563d40e3f20bd9c60358782bd9a05c00761c5732a67ca39f7323bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-362804/field-1/515effaafc563d40e3f20bd9c60358782bd9a05c00761c5732a67ca39f7323bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362804" :question/id #uuid "de94deee-b403-59ac-83e4-d5750f554710" :question/math-academy-id "q-362804" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)({csc}^{2}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-362804/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362804"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10568/selection/61c779a0c10ce06b034e039ea501deb3b92bb28d6373508e997583c536c92453" :answer/id #uuid "4b404731-de0d-5fc3-b3f5-83f572a59d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10568/selection/08593845086a497a8ea7ff072539ff307d0e764d6e948a1577d65e52c56484dc" :answer/id #uuid "5befa463-be40-57ff-aadb-0145635b25fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10568/selection/1eb3843ee81f21717cc3b9bf490c0f4c9f206aad0b91a25c1c559d3118f2c0da" :answer/id #uuid "53b54f50-d20b-5a3d-92b2-a8b8683369d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10568/selection/d93a73d7a6882f6ad0e5dfb550d97847ef2e271d34ba91b55c477b027bbe3d62" :answer/id #uuid "fd7fc5c7-6dbe-506a-bbc6-c7aa8ab30018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10568/selection/af55cfeeaf0c739443862cdae4b75921ddf03a1cc1fb58bd1b84195774aa3021" :answer/id #uuid "5061476a-e6f4-5d17-be9a-6f046a342c68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10568/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15da1347-6ea6-5d08-88f6-89994aac572d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10568/selection/08593845086a497a8ea7ff072539ff307d0e764d6e948a1577d65e52c56484dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-10568/selection/61c779a0c10ce06b034e039ea501deb3b92bb28d6373508e997583c536c92453" "q-10568/selection/08593845086a497a8ea7ff072539ff307d0e764d6e948a1577d65e52c56484dc" "q-10568/selection/1eb3843ee81f21717cc3b9bf490c0f4c9f206aad0b91a25c1c559d3118f2c0da" "q-10568/selection/d93a73d7a6882f6ad0e5dfb550d97847ef2e271d34ba91b55c477b027bbe3d62" "q-10568/selection/af55cfeeaf0c739443862cdae4b75921ddf03a1cc1fb58bd1b84195774aa3021"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10568" :question/id #uuid "53cce272-837a-502d-8e23-747f77739e8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-10568" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (9{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4}+9)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =(5x+\\pi ),$ we get \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )={sec}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (9{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4}+9)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (9[1+{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )]-5{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (9{sec}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi ))-5\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-10568/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352742/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c2f07fa9-534e-591d-ace3-f77b749601ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352742/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8df47160-cf99-5185-b531-162649f6c9fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352742/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fae646f7-d22c-514d-be75-a5d44e6ae986" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352742/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-352742/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-352742/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352742" :question/id #uuid "a57d155f-dc9a-545d-9361-c37d765e75d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-352742" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})={cos}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})|\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352742/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352714/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7a474c54-9a2c-5453-89fd-c2257bcf7595" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352714/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9298b7c0-47e2-5a26-9926-01bbe7ab3f29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352714/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-352714/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352714" :question/id #uuid "844ead48-86d3-5441-9336-ed5d8fea3ef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-352714" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})={sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352714/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352714"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10567/selection/7ed09160d82f8da07a144dc238433dd4b9fd6a034866822733a4ae4340e95323" :answer/id #uuid "05e21986-1ecc-56d8-9054-3274d697b44d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10567/selection/7e8bf80cba7f44e5aa99b9f0f059dab13eb93bc05fb3dab760c1216ed588c267" :answer/id #uuid "638f3270-f2fa-53d1-b4f2-4561b59da7b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10567/selection/e4c3cb07db0a91f22aa8083f8b38fa99ff498284a9b70a38fa0380e14ec62ad3" :answer/id #uuid "7f4c79e1-f6cb-58d1-8be6-e60bddeb1606" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10567/selection/38c70754317bbd09a8ee3b6aad08e303b2279e589b4af5ad8bb2acc5c449d255" :answer/id #uuid "7fd9b67a-76ed-56b8-bb19-8e8966dd7b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10567/selection/881009a1ebdd0d15f06133a0ef97bd9b470379b98f6454a2074c0ba524e176b8" :answer/id #uuid "2790e3f5-7ccb-5774-9136-e3aad5ed0f20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10567/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5022f738-e898-595d-b424-20d982092914" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10567/selection/881009a1ebdd0d15f06133a0ef97bd9b470379b98f6454a2074c0ba524e176b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-10567/selection/7ed09160d82f8da07a144dc238433dd4b9fd6a034866822733a4ae4340e95323" "q-10567/selection/7e8bf80cba7f44e5aa99b9f0f059dab13eb93bc05fb3dab760c1216ed588c267" "q-10567/selection/e4c3cb07db0a91f22aa8083f8b38fa99ff498284a9b70a38fa0380e14ec62ad3" "q-10567/selection/38c70754317bbd09a8ee3b6aad08e303b2279e589b4af5ad8bb2acc5c449d255" "q-10567/selection/881009a1ebdd0d15f06133a0ef97bd9b470379b98f6454a2074c0ba524e176b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10567" :question/id #uuid "11791463-1fc2-5c5f-8fd7-000137541322" :question/math-academy-id "q-10567" :question/problem "$\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =3x-2\\pi ,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7[1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi )])\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+7(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10567/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352747/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "8e2db4fb-d284-5a37-a152-0a561395610c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352747/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c594eed-22b5-57f0-92c4-70525c8a4d13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352747/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-352747/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352747" :question/id #uuid "96010cf9-9d3d-5a00-a5cc-c034a5a7c725" :question/math-academy-id "q-352747" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ with $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3{x}^{2}+4({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1))]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}+4x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{1}^{3}+4(1)]-[{0}^{3}+4(0)] \\\\  & =5-0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352747/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352747"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-477"] :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-478"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-479"] :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-480"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
